From cfc558df63dc3367d4761934d4800700568ad52c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shyalya <shyalya@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 16:19:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Trainers nobody could talk to, Survival's missing artisan
 rank, and guard directions

Three findings that turned out to be the same story: the professions added later
were never finished off.

Eighteen trainers could not be spoken to at all. creature_template.trainer_type 0
is TRAINER_TYPE_CLASS, and Creature::IsTrainerOf then compares the player's class
against trainer_class; where that is also 0 it matches nobody, since classes run
1 to 11. The function returned false for everyone and the training window never
opened. Disproportionately the expert and artisan ranks, which is why whole
professions dead-ended: Expert Blacksmith, Artisan Blacksmith, Expert Enchanter,
both Expert Survivalists.

The right value was read off the data rather than guessed. Every intact trainer
of the same skill uses trainer_type 2 - 27 for blacksmithing, 26 for tailoring,
25 for fishing, 12 for survival - and weapon masters likewise. Portal trainers use
0 with class 8; 44 of 45 hunter trainers use 0 with class 3. Naela Trance (1459)
is left alone: she is subtitled Bowyer but her rows are mage spells, so neither
value is right until her spell list is sorted out.

Survival could not pass 225. Spell 46057, the artisan rank, appears in neither
npc_trainer nor npc_trainer_template. Thirty-three items require the skill and
nine ask for more than 225 - up to four at 300 - all present and all unreachable.
Rufus Hardwick (50070) gets it: the documented artisan trainer, at Nesingwary's
Expedition, and the only survival trainer with faction 35, friendly to both sides.
Cost 50000 at skill 200 is what every profession here charges for artisan, and
level 35 continues Survival's own 1/10/20 ladder.

And no guard mentioned Survival anywhere, against thirteen entries for Herbalism.
Hellador Swiftluck (62962) is placed while we are here - a complete template with
44 trainer rows, no spawn, and faction 371, the Alah'Thalas faction, which is also
why that city had no survival trainer. His equipment_id pointed at a
creature_equip_template row that does not exist, which logged an error on every
startup once he was actually in the world; it is 0 now, as it is for every other
survival trainer. Each of the thirteen profession menus gains an entry pointing at
its nearest trainer, mapped by measuring each menu's point-of-interest centroid
against every trainer position rather than guessed.
